<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <AnalysisLevel>latest-recommended</AnalysisLevel>
    <Description>HubSpot API client for .NET</Description>
    <PackageIcon>Icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageTags>HubSpot API REST</PackageTags>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/panoramicdata/HubSpot.Api/</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/panoramicdata/HubSpot.Api</PackageProjectUrl>
    <ApplicationIcon>HubSpot.ico</ApplicationIcon>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <PackageId>HubSpot.Api</PackageId>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <NeutralLanguage>en-001</NeutralLanguage>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CA1873</NoWarn>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
      Breaking change: query filters are now request objects, and CancellationToken is mandatory.

      The major version stays at 9 because it tracks the version of the HubSpot API this library
      targets, not the shape of the library's own surface. Read the version number as "HubSpot API
      v9"; it does not follow semantic versioning, so a major version that has not moved is not a
      promise that your code still compiles. This release will not compile against existing calls.

      Endpoints that took a list of optional query parameters now take one request object:

        Before: GetPageAsync(limit: 10, properties: ["name"], cancellationToken: ct)
        After:  GetPageAsync(new CrmPageRequest { Limit = 10, Properties = ["name"] }, ct)

        Before: GetAsync(id, properties: ["name"], cancellationToken: ct)
        After:  GetAsync(id, new CrmGetRequest { Properties = ["name"] }, ct)

      CrmPageRequest derives from CrmGetRequest, adding Limit and After, so a caller that already
      has filters for one endpoint can reuse them across object types. IDomains.GetPageAsync takes
      DomainPageRequest. Where no filters are wanted, pass new().

      Every CancellationToken parameter has lost its "= default" and is now required. Calls that
      relied on the default will no longer compile; pass the token explicitly. Calls that passed it
      by name (cancellationToken: ct) still compile once the new request argument is supplied.

      The query string sent to HubSpot is unchanged: each request property carries an explicit
      AliasAs, and the outgoing URI is now covered by tests that need no portal credentials.

      Motivation: the optional parameters drew 92 static analysis findings, and the six-parameter
      filter block repeated across nine interfaces was the bulk of the library's reported code
      duplication. Both are resolved by the single shared request type.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>    <NeutralResourcesLanguage>en</NeutralResourcesLanguage>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="HubSpot.Api.Test" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="Icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
    <None Include="../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Nerdbank.GitVersioning">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Refit" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Update="Resources.Designer.cs">
      <DesignTime>True</DesignTime>
      <AutoGen>True</AutoGen>
      <DependentUpon>Resources.resx</DependentUpon>
    </Compile>
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Update="Resources.resx">
      <Generator>ResXFileCodeGenerator</Generator>
      <LastGenOutput>Resources.Designer.cs</LastGenOutput>
    </EmbeddedResource>
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <Folder Include="Interfaces\Analytics\" />
    <Folder Include="Interfaces\Auth\" />
    <Folder Include="Interfaces\Automation\" />
    <Folder Include="Interfaces\BusinessUnits\" />
    <Folder Include="Interfaces\CommunicationPreferences\" />
    <Folder Include="Interfaces\Conversations\" />
    <Folder Include="Interfaces\Events\" />
    <Folder Include="Interfaces\Webhooks\" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>